#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221939 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221431 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a65eeb21-bcd5-542d-8277-04dab7fa9b53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Inverse Laplace Transform Using the Integral Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a287c4c-314b-5a3d-a1a5-ee8569803cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493461} {:answer/id #uuid "31498a6a-f3af-5dd5-be6d-11d44f51fea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{3t}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493474} {:answer/id #uuid "44996372-2e93-5895-8ff0-6abd990cc4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(1-{e}^{3t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493505} {:answer/id #uuid "a31be869-7c0d-5e9e-bdcc-81854a7a612c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{t}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493650} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8e2fbf-32b7-580c-ac00-6c30112bdac2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31498a6a-f3af-5dd5-be6d-11d44f51fea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{3t}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493474} :answer-field/id #uuid "db0be746-6f10-5852-9c0a-08ea175957e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20b122a8-4745-5793-8bbf-3ef6f005a663" :question/math-academy-id "q-330839" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-3)},\\,s>3\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L\\{{e}^{at}\\}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\text{ }s>a.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-3)}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-3}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL\\{{e}^{at}\\}=\\frac{1}{s-a}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-3}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ\\}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{G(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{F(s)}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{3τ}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3τ}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{3t}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304857 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221431 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a65eeb21-bcd5-542d-8277-04dab7fa9b53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Inverse Laplace Transform Using the Integral Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11988bb4-bd76-5da0-89ba-38a30472093a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302571} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6e7e94-7dde-537c-98cb-20b59c24b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{6}}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302827} {:answer/id #uuid "5b39dec8-6f4d-5a1c-8367-b4a6120b8574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{{t}^{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303013} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa8899d-beae-5941-a3d4-82e94a1d2266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303108} {:answer/id #uuid "e6893c52-98ee-5b15-a3f0-a746742b6299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6aa8899d-beae-5941-a3d4-82e94a1d2266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303108} :answer-field/id #uuid "95522057-6f76-5a8c-85b6-0d8377b32c14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c43f625b-d110-5aef-9243-2a1cae536c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-330843" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{6}},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L\\{{t}^{n}\\}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{6}}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{n}\\}=\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{4!}{{s}^{4+1}}\\} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ\\}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{G(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{F(s)}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{τ}^{4}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221431 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a65eeb21-bcd5-542d-8277-04dab7fa9b53" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Inverse Laplace Transform Using the Integral Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b30fb93-d4f5-57ff-89d5-4ae27e848f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302824} {:answer/id #uuid "45bc93fe-5bb2-55dd-8c94-74f48290abdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(1-{e}^{5t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302897} {:answer/id #uuid "69b71edb-5681-5b89-9393-9ba3e46b6fbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{t}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303100} {:answer/id #uuid "75e53d4a-6a6b-5a91-815b-dc87331bce6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{5t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303176} {:answer/id #uuid "7906a1bc-f57e-5117-b624-76a26363e3f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7906a1bc-f57e-5117-b624-76a26363e3f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303204} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c0df3ef-2be2-59de-94c6-d27577149ad2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8064a487-d480-5cc5-97a5-d474531a9775" :question/math-academy-id "q-330849" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)},\\,s>5\n$$\n\nfind the inverse Laplace transform of $G(s),$ given that\n$L\\{{e}^{at}\\}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\text{ }s>a.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we can write $G(s)$ as \n\n$$\nG(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s-5)}=\\frac{F(s)}{s},\n$$\n\nwhere $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-5}.$\nAlso, we know that\n\n$$\nL\\{{e}^{at}\\}=\\frac{1}{s-a}.\n$$\n\nThus, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{F(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & ={e}^{5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we know that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$, then\n\n$$\nL\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ\\}=\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\n$$\n\nUsing the property above in reverse, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}\\{G(s)\\} & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{F(s)}{s}\\} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{5τ}\\,\\text{d}τ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{e}^{5τ}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({e}^{5t}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370100 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221432 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "51dfecdb-ad66-5e07-8873-ca8e116b27bd" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Formula for Laplace Transforms of Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94356250-04c6-5d39-ba5d-7e4b6a1c3617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370102} {:answer/id #uuid "6af64c5a-daef-5659-9f22-bad50ed6662a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370103} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a6a761-7eaf-5b3f-b44c-2cc2163e8b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370104} {:answer/id #uuid "c4bde22b-1104-5a4c-8e72-8083b2a7721a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0a6a761-7eaf-5b3f-b44c-2cc2163e8b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370104} :answer-field/id #uuid "10807e40-8603-55ae-8902-22cd7325d252" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/re